Learnings from SecurePay MCP Integration:

1. Authentication Flow:
- Uses OAuth 2.0 with client credentials flow
- OAuth endpoint: https://welcome.api2.sandbox.auspost.com.au/oauth/token
- Required grant_type=client_credentials and audience=https://api.payments.auspost.com.au
- Access tokens valid for 24 hours (86400 seconds)
- Basic auth header must be correctly base64 encoded

2. API Endpoints:
- Sandbox base URL: https://payments-stest.npe.auspost.zone
- Payment endpoints use XML API (/xmlapi/payment)
- Must use PUT method instead of POST for payment requests
- Content-Type should be application/vnd.securepay+xml

3. Payment Flow:
- Two-step process: initialize payment then process with card details
- Message ID used to track the payment through the flow
- Amounts must be in cents (multiply by 100)
- XML payloads require specific format:
  - SecurePayMessage wrapper
  - MessageInfo with ID and timestamp
  - MerchantInfo with credentials
  - Payment section with TxnList

4. Common Issues:
- Method Not Allowed (405) when using POST instead of PUT
- Access Denied (403) when authorization header missing
- Invalid Argument for incorrect auth formatting
- XML format must be exact and well-formed

5. Required Fields:
- messageID: unique identifier (using timestamp)
- messageTimestamp: ISO format
- apiVersion: xml-4.2
- txnType: 0 for payment
- txnSource: 23 for API

6. Environment Variables:
SECUREPAY_MERCHANT_ID=5AR0055
SECUREPAY_MERCHANT_CODE=5AR0055
SECUREPAY_PASSWORD=[client_id:client_secret]
SECUREPAY_SANDBOX_URL=https://payments-stest.npe.auspost.zone
SECUREPAY_OAUTH_URL=https://welcome.api2.sandbox.auspost.com.au/oauth/token
SECUREPAY_CLIENT_ID=[your-client-id]
SECUREPAY_CLIENT_SECRET=[your-client-secret]